Usages:
  query_serving_boundary: |
    RequestHandler dispatches Prometheus-API-compatible paths (/api/v1/query,
    /api/v1/query_range, /api/v1/series, /api/v1/labels, /api/v1/export, /federate, ...) to the
    prometheus subpackage, and Graphite-compatible paths (/render, /metrics/find, /tags, ...) to
    the graphite subpackage. Both ultimately call into the netstorage subpackage
    (ProcessSearchQuery and friends), which in this pinned single-binary commit calls the
    storage-facing cell's in-process facade (vmstorage.GetSearch / vmstorage.VMSelectAPI) rather
    than a networked vmselect-to-vmstorage RPC — the RPC server/client scaffolding exists
    (lib/vmselectapi.Server/.Client) but no code path in this repository snapshot exercises the
    client side. promql supplies MetricsQL/PromQL expression evaluation and a rollup-result
    cache consumed by the prometheus subpackage's query handlers.

Annotations: |
  This cell is the query-serving boundary: it owns the Prometheus- and Graphite-compatible HTTP
  API surface and composes the promql (expression evaluation) and netstorage (result-fan-out)
  subpackages to answer queries. As with the ingestion-side cells in this forest, its own
  top-level exported functions carry no cross-cell-typed parameters, so its real dependency on
  lib/promscrape (status/config endpoints) and the storage-facing cell (via netstorage, out of
  this cell's own directory scope) is described here in prose.

  Use `query_serving_boundary` to understand what "fan-out" actually means in this pinned commit
  versus in a genuinely distributed cluster deployment.

---

"Init(vmselectMaxConcurrentRequests: int, vmselectMaxQueueDuration: time.Duration)":
  location: main.go
  annotations: |
    Prepare the query-serving subsystem before the first request can be handled.

    Algorithm:
    1. Initialize the temporary-blocks spill directory used by netstorage's fan-out buffering
    2. Initialize promql's rollup-result cache
    3. Build a bounded concurrency-limiting channel sized by `vmselectMaxConcurrentRequests`,
       queuing beyond it for at most `vmselectMaxQueueDuration` before rejecting a request
    4. Initialize the embedded VMUI static-asset configuration and the vmalert HTTP proxy

"RequestHandler(w: HTTPResponseWriter, r: HTTPRequest) -> handled:bool":
  location: main.go
  annotations: |
    Route one incoming HTTP request by URL path to the matching Prometheus-API or
    Graphite-API handler, or serve an embedded VMUI/static asset, returning false for
    unrecognized paths.

    Use `query_serving_boundary` for the full route-to-subpackage mapping.

"Stop()":
  location: main.go
  annotations: |
    Release resources acquired by `Init` (temporary-blocks directory, caches).

"InitSecretFlags()":
  location: main.go
  annotations: |
    Register command-line flags whose values must never be logged/exposed on the /flags
    debug endpoint (e.g. auth tokens embedded in remote data-source URLs, if configured).

